{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>They piled up, etc.; they stood, etc.; they froze, etc.</b> The meaning is: corresponding to three miracles that HaShem performed at the sea: First, that the waters split and all gathered together and were no longer scattered in the open space, but all became a single heap to make a path for the feet of Israel. Second, the waters that would converge and come pouring into the sea from the sides stood upright in the place where the first ones had piled up — and this is what is meant by <b>they stood like a wall of flowing water</b> — meaning, those that flow and come stood like a wall. Third, according to what we have already brought up (Exodus 14:21), that the entire sea was not split, so that they would not need to descend into the depths of the sea — the part that was not split froze and became like dry land, and corresponding to this it says ״they froze, etc.״ And I have already written that the freezing preceded the splitting, and this is what is meant by <b>the depths froze in the heart of the sea</b> — before it was torn open, its heart froze, and from its heart upward remained water that did not freeze and was split. And the reason it says <b>depths</b> in the plural — according to the Sages, of blessed memory (Exodus Rabbah 24:1), who said that the sea was split into twelve passages, and every place that was split, there the deep froze — and corresponding to all of them it says <b>depths.</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:22.469960200Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}